\"used_as\":\"printf argument with format %s\"}],\"calls\":[\"printf\",\"__isoc99_scanf\"],\"notes\":\"Same signed JL index check as edit_cookie. Negative/large uint64 index passes check. msg[index] is dereferenced and printed as a string, enabling potential OOB read.\"},{\"name\":\"menu\",\"address\":\"0x17fd\",\"callers\":[\"main\"],\"callees\":[\"puts\",\"__stack_chk_fail\"],\"inputs\":[],\"checks\":[],\"memory_operations\":[],\"calls\":[\"puts\"]},{\"name\":\"_abort\",\"address\":\"0x11f5\",\"callers\":[\"init\",\"create_cookie\",\"eat_cookie\",\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\"],\"callees\":[\"printf\",\"exit\"],\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"msg\",\"source\":\"rdi\",\"type\":\"string\"}],\"checks\":[],\"memory_operations\":[],\"calls\":[\"printf\",\"exit\"]}],\"attack_surfaces\":[{\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"input\":\"cookie_index (scanf %llu)\",\"operation\":\"WRITE to msg[index] with size msg_size[index]-1\",\"risk\":\"HIGH\",\"reason\":\"Attacker-controlled index has NO lower-bound check (only signed JL against cookie_num). Negative index reaches OOB memory before msg[] and msg_size[] arrays. The OOB msg_size value controls read length, and the OOB msg value is dereferenced as the write destination. This gives attacker-controlled arbitrary write primitive if suitable OOB values exist.\"},{\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"input\":\"cookie_index (scanf %llu)\",\"operation\":\"READ msg[index] and printf(%s, msg[index])\",\"risk\":\"HIGH\",\"reason\":\"Same missing lower-bound check on index. OOB msg[index] is dereferenced and printed as string, enabling potential info leak from arbitrary memory if a valid pointer can be reached at a negative offset.\"},{\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"input\":\"random_index (urandom % cookie_num)\",\"operation\":\"FREE msg[random_index] then swap-with-last\",\"risk\":\"MEDIUM\",\"reason\":\"When random_index == cookie_num-1, the freed pointer is self-assigned back (not NULLed), leaving a dangling pointer. However, index is random (not attacker-controlled), so triggering the specific case requires probability. After free, cookie_num decrements, and the dangling slot is at index cookie_num (now out of valid range for edit/read, but the swap logic itself may have issues).\"},{\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"input\":\"message_size (scanf %lld)\",\"operation\":\"ALLOC calloc(size,1) + read(0, buf, size)\",\"risk\":\"LOW\",\"reason\":\"Size is checked <= 0x100. calloc zero-initializes. No obvious overflow. Size stored as int32 in msg_size[].\"}],\"facts\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Binary is PIE-enabled, Full RELRO, NX, Canary, not stripped, amd64\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F002\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"libc is glibc 2.39 (Ubuntu 2.39-0ubuntu8.8) at /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6\",\"source\":\"RUNTIME\"},{\"id\":\"F003\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg[] is a pointer array of 32 elements (8 bytes each) at BSS 0x4060, size 256 bytes\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F004\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg_size[] is an int32 array of 32 elements at BSS 0x4160, size 128 bytes\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F005\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"cookie_num is int64 at BSS 0x41e8, initialized to 5 by init()\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F006\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"init() pre-allocates 5 cookies via strdup with sizes 0x50, 0x30, 0x18, 0x38, 0x40\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F007\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"create_cookie checks cookie_num <= 0x1f and size <= 0x100, uses calloc(size,1) then read(0,buf,size)\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F008\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie reads index via scanf(%llu) at 0x1671, compares with signed JL at 0x1681 (cmp rdx,rax; jl). No lower-bound (>=0) check exists.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F009\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie uses index to read msg_size[index] (at 0x16a7, lea rdx,[rax*4] + msg_size base) as read length minus 1, and msg[index] (at 0x16c3, lea rcx,[rax*8] + msg base) as write destination for read(0, ptr, len)\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F010\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"read_cookie reads index via scanf(%llu) at 0x179a, compares with signed JL at 0x17aa. No lower-bound check. Uses msg[index] as printf %s argument.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F011\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie selects random index via fread(/dev/urandom) % cookie_num, frees msg[idx], then copies msg[cookie_num-1] into msg[idx] and msg_size[cookie_num-1] into msg_size[idx], decrements cookie_num\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F012\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie does not NULL the freed pointer when idx == cookie_num-1 (self-assignment case); the slot at old cookie_num-1 retains the freed pointer value but is now outside [0, new_cookie_num-1]\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F013\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"BSS layout: stdout(0x4020,8) stdin(0x4030,8) stderr(0x4040,8) gap(0x4048-0x405f) msg[32](0x4060-0x415f) msg_size[32](0x4160-0x41df) urandom(0x41e0,8) cookie_num(0x41e8,8)\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F014\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"scanf format for menu choice is %lld (int64), for edit/read index is %llu (uint64)\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F015\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"alarm(60) is called in init(), setting a 60-second timeout\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F016\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie and read_cookie index check uses signed JL (jump if less, signed). A uint64 value like 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF (-1 signed) passes the check since -1 < cookie_num (5). The index is then used in LEA with rax*8/rax*4 scaling, computing addresses before msg[] base.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F017\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"With negative index in edit_cookie, msg_size[neg] reads from memory before 0x4160 (i.e., within msg[] array or earlier BSS), and msg[neg] reads from memory before 0x4060 (i.e., stderr/stdin/stdout pointers or earlier). The read size and write destination are both attacker-influenced via OOB.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F018\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"With negative index in read_cookie, msg[neg] reads a pointer from before 0x4060 and passes it to printf(%s), potentially leaking memory content if the OOB value is a valid pointer.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"id\":\"U001\",\"description\":\"Whether CET (IBT/SHSTK) is enabled at runtime\",\"reason\":\"checksec does not report CET flags; kernel/config dependent\"},{\"id\":\"U002\",\"description\":\"Whether seccomp or other sandbox is active\",\"reason\":\"No seccomp-related symbols or prctl calls found in binary, but external sandbox cannot be ruled out from static analysis alone\"},{\"id\":\"U003\",\"description\":\"Exact heap layout and tcache behavior under glibc 2.39 for the specific allocation sizes used (0x50, 0x30, 0x18, 0x38, 0x40 and user-controlled <=0x100)\",\"reason\":\"Requires dynamic heap analysis to determine chunk alignment and tcache bin placement\"},{\"id\":\"U004\",\"description\":\"Whether the eat_cookie self-assignment dangling pointer is practically reachable and exploitable given the random index\",\"reason\":\"Index is random from /dev/urandom; triggering idx==cookie_num-1 requires 1/N probability per call, needs dynamic verification\"}],\"raw\":{\"elf\":\"ELF64 LSB PIE, x86-64, dynamically linked, interpreter /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, BuildID=84dab319bf6fe22134cf0338cbd8071fd8bc06c2, not stripped. Entry=0x1110. 11 program headers, 29 sections.\",\"sections\":\".text(0x1110,0x891,AX) .rodata(0x2000,0x266,A) .data(0x4000,0x10,WA) .bss(0x4020,0x1d0,WA) .got(0x3f58,0xa8,WA) .plt(0x1020,0xe0,AX) .init_array(0x3d58,0x8,WA) .fini_array(0x3d60,0x8,WA) .dynamic(0x3d68,0x1f0,WA)\",\"symbols\":\"main(0x187f) init(0x1232) create_cookie(0x1399) eat_cook